---
import ToolLayout from '../../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';

const faqEntries = [
  {
    q: "What does a JSON formatter do?",
    a: "A JSON formatter takes raw or compressed JSON and adds consistent indentation and line breaks so you can actually read it. This tool parses your input with the browser's native JSON.parse, then re-serializes it with your chosen indent level."
  },
  {
    q: "What is the difference between formatting and minifying JSON?",
    a: "Formatting (pretty-printing) adds whitespace, indentation, and newlines to make JSON human-readable. Minifying strips all unnecessary whitespace to produce the smallest possible output. Both operations preserve the data exactly as-is."
  },
  {
    q: "How does JSON validation work here?",
    a: "When you click Format or Minify, the tool runs JSON.parse on your input. If parsing fails, you get the exact error message from the JavaScript engine, including the character position where it broke. Valid JSON is re-serialized to the output panel."
  },
  {
    q: "Does it support nested objects and arrays?",
    a: "Yes. Any valid JSON structure works, including deeply nested objects, arrays of arrays, mixed types, and large documents. The formatter handles the full JSON spec."
  },
  {
    q: "Is it safe to paste sensitive or private JSON?",
    a: "Yes. Everything runs client-side in your browser. Your JSON is never sent to a server, never logged, and never stored. Close the tab and it is gone."
  },
  {
    q: "Is there a size or character limit?",
    a: "There is no hard limit set by the tool. Practical limits depend on your browser and available memory. Most browsers handle several megabytes of JSON without issues."
  },
  {
    q: "What do the error messages mean?",
    a: "Error messages come directly from your browser's JSON parser. Common ones include 'Unexpected token' (syntax error at a specific position), 'Unexpected end of JSON input' (truncated or incomplete data), and 'Expected property name' (missing quotes around keys)."
  },
  {
    q: "How is this different from using jq on the command line?",
    a: "jq is a query and transformation language for JSON. This tool focuses on formatting, minifying, and validating. If you just need to pretty-print or check syntax, this is faster than opening a terminal. For filtering or reshaping data, jq is the better choice."
  }
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqEntries.map(e => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": e.q,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": e.a
    }
  }))
};

const softwareJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
  "name": "JSON Formatter & Validator",
  "url": "https://toolblip.com/tools/json-formatter/",
  "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
  "operatingSystem": "Any (browser-based)",
  "offers": {
    "@type": "Offer",
    "price": "0",
    "priceCurrency": "USD"
  },
  "description": "Format, validate, and minify JSON instantly in your browser. Highlights errors, supports 2 or 4-space indent. Free, no sign-up."
};

const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Home",
      "item": "https://toolblip.com/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 2,
      "name": "Tools",
      "item": "https://toolblip.com/tools/"
    },
    {
      "@type": "ListItem",
      "position": 3,
      "name": "JSON Formatter",
      "item": "https://toolblip.com/tools/json-formatter/"
    }
  ]
};
---

<ToolLayout
  title="JSON Formatter & Validator Online Free — Toolblip"
  description="Format, validate, and minify JSON instantly in your browser. Highlights errors, supports 2 or 4-space indent. Free — no sign-up."
  toolSlug="json-formatter"
  category="developer"
>
  <Fragment slot="jsonld">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqJsonLd)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(softwareJsonLd)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbJsonLd)} />
  </Fragment>

  <div class="flex gap-2 mb-3">
    <button id="jf-format" class="bg-green-600 hover:bg-green-500 text-white text-sm font-medium px-4 py-1.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Format</button>
    <button id="jf-minify" class="bg-gray-700 hover:bg-gray-600 text-white text-sm font-medium px-4 py-1.5 rounded-lg transition-colors">Minify</button>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-auto text-sm text-gray-400">
      Indent:
      <label class="flex items-center gap-1 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="indent" value="2" checked class="accent-green-500"> 2</label>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-1 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="indent" value="4" class="accent-green-500"> 4</label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
    <div>
      <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mb-1">Input</div>
      <textarea
        id="jf-input"
        class="w-full h-64 bg-gray-800 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-gray-100 text-sm font-mono resize-y focus:outline-none focus:border-green-500 placeholder-gray-500"
        placeholder='{"key": "value"}'
      ></textarea>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-500">Output</span>
        <button id="jf-copy" class="text-xs text-green-400 hover:text-green-300 transition-colors">Copy</button>
      </div>
      <textarea
        id="jf-output"
        readonly
        class="w-full h-64 bg-gray-800 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-3 text-gray-100 text-sm font-mono resize-y focus:outline-none"
        placeholder="Formatted JSON will appear here..."
      ></textarea>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="jf-error" class="hidden mt-2 text-sm text-red-400 bg-red-900/20 border border-red-800 rounded-lg px-3 py-2"></div>

  <script>
    const inputEl = document.getElementById('jf-input') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
    const outputEl = document.getElementById('jf-output') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
    const errorEl = document.getElementById('jf-error')!;
    const copyBtn = document.getElementById('jf-copy')!;
    const formatBtn = document.getElementById('jf-format')!;
    const minifyBtn = document.getElementById('jf-minify')!;

    function getIndent() {
      return parseInt((document.querySelector('input[name="indent"]:checked') as HTMLInputElement)?.value ?? '2');
    }

    function showError(msg: string) {
      errorEl.textContent = msg;
      errorEl.classList.remove('hidden');
      outputEl.value = '';
    }

    function hideError() { errorEl.classList.add('hidden'); }

    function parse() {
      const raw = inputEl.value.trim();
      if (!raw) { outputEl.value = ''; hideError(); return null; }
      try { const parsed = JSON.parse(raw); hideError(); return parsed; }
      catch (e: any) { showError(`Invalid JSON: ${e.message}`); return null; }
    }

    formatBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const parsed = parse();
      if (parsed !== null) outputEl.value = JSON.stringify(parsed, null, getIndent());
    });

    minifyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const parsed = parse();
      if (parsed !== null) outputEl.value = JSON.stringify(parsed);
    });

    copyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      if (!outputEl.value) return;
      navigator.clipboard.writeText(outputEl.value).then(() => {
        copyBtn.textContent = 'Copied!';
        setTimeout(() => { copyBtn.textContent = 'Copy'; }, 2000);
      });
    });

    // Auto-format on paste
    inputEl.addEventListener('paste', () => {
      setTimeout(() => {
        const parsed = parse();
        if (parsed !== null) outputEl.value = JSON.stringify(parsed, null, getIndent());
      }, 10);
    });
  </script>

  <div slot="howto">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3">How to use</h2>
    <ol class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-2 list-decimal list-inside">
      <li>Paste or type your JSON into the input panel on the left. The tool also auto-formats when you paste.</li>
      <li>Pick your indent size (2 or 4 spaces) using the radio buttons in the toolbar.</li>
      <li>Click <strong class="text-white">Format</strong> to pretty-print the JSON, or <strong class="text-white">Minify</strong> to strip all whitespace.</li>
      <li>If the JSON is invalid, an error message appears below the panels with the exact parse failure and position.</li>
      <li>Click <strong class="text-white">Copy</strong> above the output panel to copy the result to your clipboard.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <div slot="description">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-2">JSON formatter online: format, validate, and minify</h2>
    <div class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed space-y-3">
      <p>This json formatter online tool takes raw JSON and turns it into something readable. Paste a minified API response, a config file, or any JSON blob, and it pretty-prints it with consistent indentation. You can choose between 2-space and 4-space indent depending on your preference or project style.</p>
      <p>The minify mode does the opposite: it strips every unnecessary space, newline, and tab to give you the smallest valid JSON string. Useful when you need to stuff JSON into a URL parameter, a single-line config value, or anywhere size matters.</p>
      <p>Validation happens automatically. When you click Format or Minify, the tool parses your input using the browser's built-in JSON parser. If something is wrong, you get the exact error message with the character position where parsing failed. No vague "invalid input" messages. You see the same error you would get in a browser console, which makes it straightforward to find and fix the problem.</p>
      <p>Everything runs in your browser. Your JSON never leaves your machine, never hits a server, and is never stored or logged anywhere. This matters when you are working with tokens, credentials, user data, or anything you would not want in someone else's logs.</p>
      <p>The tool auto-formats on paste, so you can skip the extra click in most cases. Output copies to clipboard with one button. No accounts, no rate limits, no ads.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div slot="faq">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-4 mt-8">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      {faqEntries.map(entry => (
        <details class="group">
          <summary class="text-sm font-medium text-gray-200 cursor-pointer hover:text-white transition-colors">{entry.q}</summary>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed mt-2 pl-4">{entry.a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div slot="related">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-3 mt-8">Related tools</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <a href="/tools/base64/" class="text-sm bg-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-700 border border-gray-700 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">Base64 Encode/Decode</a>
      <a href="/tools/url-encode/" class="text-sm bg-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-700 border border-gray-700 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">URL Encode/Decode</a>
      <a href="/tools/markdown-to-html/" class="text-sm bg-gray-800 hover:bg-gray-700 border border-gray-700 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg text-gray-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">Markdown to HTML</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</ToolLayout>
